---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
import VideoSection from '../../components/VideoSection.astro';
import Infographic from '../../components/Infographic.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n/ui';
import type { Lang } from '../../i18n/utils';

const lang: Lang = 'en';
---
<Base lang={lang} path="/events/alliance-duel/" title="Alliance Duel: Complete Guide" description="Six days of point categories, a Saturday PvP finale, phase-by-phase mechanics with exact point values, Falcon Quest stacking, and the save-everything economy that wins the top chest.">
  <GuidePage title="Alliance Duel: Complete Guide" description="Six days of point categories, a Saturday PvP finale, phase-by-phase mechanics with exact point values, Falcon Quest stacking, and the save-everything economy that wins the top chest." lang={lang}>
    <p>The Alliance Duel is the event the whole week is built around: six days of competition against a matched rival alliance, with a different point category every day and a PvP finale on Saturday. It is also the event that decides how much of your stash you should ever spend — shards, tickets, badges and speedups all have a duel day where they are worth double or more.</p>
    <p>This guide covers entry requirements, the phase mechanics with exact point values, the daily saving strategy, Falcon Quest stacking, and how the duel feeds into Kingdom War.</p>

    <h2 id="what-it-is">What the Alliance Duel Is</h2>
    <p>The Alliance Duel is a <strong>6-day alliance competition</strong> divided into phases 1 through 6, running Monday to Saturday. Each day has its own point category — a specific set of actions that earns duel points — and the alliance that scores more in the daily category wins that phase. Saturday, Phase 6, is the <strong>PvP finale</strong> where the two alliances finally fight each other directly.</p>
    <p>There is also a compressed format: <strong>Survival Battle</strong>, a 4-hour version of the duel for alliances that want the same competition without the full week. The mechanics and scoring logic are identical — only the clock changes.</p>
    <blockquote>The duel is not won on the day. It is won by whoever saved the right resources for the right phase.</blockquote>

    <h2 id="entry-requirements">Entry Requirements and Matchmaking</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your alliance must be a <strong>top-32 ranked alliance</strong> with <strong>20 or more members</strong> to enter.</li>
      <li>On a brand-new server, the first duel runs around <strong>day 17</strong> — plan your opening two weeks around it.</li>
      <li>After Phase 6 ends there is a <strong>1-day break</strong> before the next cycle begins.</li>
      <li>Matchmaking is believed to be based on <strong>alliance activity and win rate</strong> — highly active alliances get paired against similarly active ones, not purely by raw power.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="weekly-structure">The Week at a Glance</h2>
    <table class="w-full mb-6 text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Day</th><th>Phase</th><th>Focus</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Monday</td><td>Phase 1</td><td>Daily point category — check the event screen for the exact scoring actions</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Tuesday</td><td>Phase 2</td><td>Daily point category — same, the categories rotate per day</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Wednesday</td><td>Phase 3</td><td>Research and scroll day</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Thursday</td><td>Phase 4</td><td>Heroes and recruitment</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Friday</td><td>Phase 5</td><td>Troop training</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Saturday</td><td>Phase 6</td><td>PvP finale against the rival alliance</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Phases 1 and 2 change their categories from cycle to cycle, so read the in-game event screen each week. Phases 3, 4 and 5 are the big planning days — the ones where hoarding pays — and they are covered in detail below.</p>
    <Infographic src="/infographics/duel-day-guide.webp" alt="Alliance Duel day-by-day guide with icons — what to save and what to spend each phase" caption="The duel week at a glance — save for the right phase, spend on the right day" />

    <h2 id="phase-3">Phase 3: Research and Scroll Day</h2>
    <p>Phase 3 scores your research activity, but it has a trap built in: <strong>scroll points are only awarded for scrolls consumed on that day.</strong> Burning scrolls on Monday earns nothing on Wednesday.</p>
    <p>The workaround is to research things that <strong>do not cost scrolls</strong>:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Hero research</strong> — full point value, zero scroll cost.</li>
      <li><strong>Soldier research</strong> — same deal, and it compounds into Phase 5 troop value.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Two chest rules complete the day:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Raven gear chests are promoted</strong> during Phase 3 — the event awards points for <strong>opening</strong> them. This is the day to crack your stash.</li>
      <li><strong>Curio chests give no points</strong> in the duel — but they have no time pressure either. Claim them whenever you like; nothing is lost by saving them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="phase-4">Phase 4: Heroes and Recruitment</h2>
    <p>Phase 4 is the highest-value day for hero assets. The exact point values:</p>
    <table class="w-full mb-6 text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Action</th><th>Points</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>1 UR shard</td><td>+20,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>SSR shard</td><td>+7,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>SR shard</td><td>+2,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Recruitment</td><td>+3,450</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Skill badge</td><td>+20</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>One UR shard alone is worth nearly six SSRs. That math drives the whole week: <strong>save your recruitment tickets, hero shards and skill badges for Phase 4.</strong> Spending shards the day you get them is throwing away the single biggest point multiplier the duel offers.</p>

    <h2 id="phase-5">Phase 5: Troop Training</h2>
    <p>Phase 5 converts your barracks output into points:</p>
    <table class="w-full mb-6 text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Source</th><th>Points</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Trained soldier, Tier 1</td><td>+46</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Trained soldier, Tier 10</td><td>+253</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Training Boost</td><td>+115 per minute</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Tier values scale between the two endpoints — higher tiers pay several times what T1s do, so train the highest tier your barracks support. And the event stacks its own bonuses on top for the day:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>All points +100%</strong> — everything earned on Phase 5 day is doubled.</li>
      <li><strong>Speedups +30%</strong> — speedup efficiency is boosted.</li>
      <li><strong>Training +30%</strong> — training itself runs faster.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The conclusion is obvious: <strong>save your training speedups for Phase 5.</strong> A speedup burned on a random Tuesday is worth 30% less and earns half the points.</p>

    <h2 id="sunday-planning">Sunday: The Pre-Planning Day</h2>
    <p>The break day after Phase 6 is not a rest day — it is the planning day for the next cycle. Before the new duel starts:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Check your stash: shards, tickets, badges, speedups, Raven gear chests, curio chests.</li>
      <li>Assign each stockpile to the phase that pays for it — Phase 3, 4 or 5.</li>
      <li>Set the alliance goal: the target is the <strong>maximum milestone chest</strong> and the top promotions the roster can reach.</li>
      <li>Check your <strong>Alliance Duel Technology</strong> — at 100% it changes what goals are realistic, so leadership should know exactly where the alliance stands before committing to a target.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="falcon-quest-stacking">Falcon Quest Stacking</h2>
    <p>Falcon Quests interact with the duel through one rule: <strong>do the quests whenever you like, but claim them on double-point days — Monday, Wednesday and Friday.</strong> A claimed quest on the wrong day earns half of what it could.</p>
    <p>Then the advanced trick, the <strong>Stacking Max - 1</strong> technique:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>When your quest board is completely full, the board timer <strong>freezes</strong> — no new quests arrive while it is full.</li>
      <li>Keep the board at max minus one instead: complete one quest, and the timer keeps running, refreshing the board.</li>
      <li>The result is a continuous quest pipeline instead of a frozen one, and far more quests banked for the double-point days.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="new-server-notes">New Server Notes</h2>
    <p>Two calendar facts every new server player should know:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>There is no raid during the first 2 weeks</strong> of a new server. Raid content starts in <strong>week 3</strong> — do not burn resources expecting it earlier.</li>
      <li>The <strong>first Alliance Duel lands around day 17</strong>. The opening-two-weeks economy in the beginner guides is tuned exactly to this: build up, then have something worth scoring when the first duel opens.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="rewards">Rewards and the KvK Connection</h2>
    <p>Duel payouts come in two layers:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Milestone chests</strong> — the alliance goal is always the maximum chest. Everything else is secondary.</li>
      <li><strong>Promotions and contribution ranking</strong> — individual rewards scale with your personal contribution, which is why solo hoarding that never gets spent helps nobody.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>And the duel is not an isolated event: it feeds directly into <strong>Kingdom War</strong>. <a href="/events/kvk/">KvK</a> and the duel share scoring sources — <strong>Covert Ops and Caravans score for both</strong>. Run them every day and the same effort pays twice. The full caravan route is covered in the <a href="/events/wagon/">Guild Wagon and Caravans guide</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="common-mistakes">Common Mistakes</h2>
    <Infographic src="/infographics/duel-savings.webp" alt="Alliance Duel savings guide — what to stockpile for each duel phase" caption="The savings plan: stockpile checklist per phase" />
    <ol>
      <li>Spending shards and tickets outside Phase 4 — the single biggest point loss in the event.</li>
      <li>Burning training speedups outside Phase 5 and losing the +100% day bonus.</li>
      <li>Consuming scrolls for research on non-scroll days instead of running scroll-free hero and soldier research.</li>
      <li>Claiming Falcon Quests on single-point days.</li>
      <li>Letting the quest board freeze at full instead of keeping it one slot short.</li>
      <li>Ignoring the 1-day break after Phase 6 and showing up to the new cycle unprepared.</li>
    </ol>

    <VideoSection topic="alliance_duel" lang={lang} />
  </GuidePage>
</Base>
